# PostgressOps MCP Bootstrap

When the user connects `postgres-ops` MCP or asks to set up PostgreSQL ops on a remote server:

## Read config first

Check `~/.cursor/mcp.json` for:
- `mcpServers.postgres-ops.args` — SSH user@host
- `mcpServers.postgres-ops.postgressops.installPath` or env `POSTGRESSOPS_HOME` in remote command
- `_postgressops` block — repo URL and bootstrap steps

Default install path: **`/opt/postgressops`** (override per user in mcp.json).

Repository: **https://github.com/Makmillerme/postgressops.git**

## Bootstrap on server (if stack missing or MCP fails)

```bash
export POSTGRESSOPS_HOME="${POSTGRESSOPS_HOME:-/opt/postgressops}"
export POSTGRESSOPS_REPO="https://github.com/Makmillerme/postgressops.git"
git clone "$POSTGRESSOPS_REPO" "$POSTGRESSOPS_HOME"  # skip if exists
cd "$POSTGRESSOPS_HOME"
cp docker/.env.example docker/.env   # user fills secrets
bash scripts/server-update.sh
```

## MCP remote command (preferred after install)

```text
POSTGRESSOPS_HOME=/opt/postgressops POSTGRESSOPS_REPO=https://github.com/Makmillerme/postgressops.git \
  bash /opt/postgressops/scripts/mcp-ssh-entrypoint.sh
```

## After path change

Update both:
- `POSTGRESSOPS_HOME` in `~/.cursor/mcp.json` remote SSH command
- `STACK_DIR` / `SCRIPTS_DIR` in `tools/mcp-postgres-ops/.env` (auto-set by `server-update.sh`)
